IMPORT prelude

-- Public Transport Council Act 1987 (Singapore) -- fare evasion and the penalty fee (ss 2 "invalid ticket", 52-54, 57, 58), the
-- evidentiary certificate (s 55(9), (10)), non-payment of taxi and ride-hail fares (s 56), charging fares (s 41), unlicensed ticket
-- payment services (ss 28, 64), the Fuel Equalisation Fund penalty (s 33), appeals (s 40), composition (s 67) and the fare
-- adjustment formula (s 49, Third Schedule).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PTCA1987.txt. The edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; later amendments are shown to Act 17 of 2025 (wef 23
-- September 2026) and S 669/2025 (wef 9 October 2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what a passenger, driver, operator or
-- payment-service provider meets. Not encoded: the Council's constitution, functions and finances (Parts 2-4), licence conditions,
-- codes of practice and suspension (ss 29-31, 34-39), street-hail and ride-hail pricing policy orders (ss 43-46), the procedure for
-- approving and reviewing fares (ss 47, 48), contributions from fare increases (s 50), investigations (Part 10), offences by bodies
-- corporate (s 65), and the prescribed amount of the penalty fee, which is left to regulations not deposited.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Transport Council Act 1987 -- fares`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF a < b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `2 -- invalid ticket`

-- s 2: "invalid ticket" means a ticket for a journey on a public bus or licensed rapid transit train (a) used or attempted to be
-- used (i) for a journey not the one for which it was issued; (ii) "to over-travel the fare that was paid for the journey, without
-- reasonable excuse"; or (iii) by a person who is not the first user of a non-transferable ticket; (b) altered or defaced; (c)
-- counterfeit; or (d) expired.
DECLARE TicketState IS ONE OF
    `a ticket in order`
    `a ticket used for a different journey`
    `a ticket used to over-travel without reasonable excuse`
    `a ticket used to over-travel with a reasonable excuse`
    `a non-transferable ticket used by someone other than its first user`
    `an altered or defaced ticket`
    `a counterfeit ticket`
    `an expired ticket`

GIVEN `the ticket` IS A TicketState
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ticket is invalid` IF
    CONSIDER `the ticket`
    WHEN `a ticket in order` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a ticket used to over-travel with a reasonable excuse` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `54(4) -- what counts as evading a fare`

-- s 54(4): an individual evades payment of a fare if (a) when ATTEMPTING to travel (including entering a paid area), without
-- reasonable excuse, he (i) does not pay; (ii) with a smartcard, "does not tap in"; (iii) uses a concession fare without
-- entitlement; or (iv) uses an invalid ticket; (b) for a journey TRAVELLED, without reasonable excuse, (i) does not pay; (ii) with a
-- smartcard, "does not tap in or tap out"; (iii) concession without entitlement; (iv) invalid ticket; or (c) a prescribed act or
-- omission. s 54(1) and s 53(1) apply only to a bus "provided by a public bus operator" or a train "provided by a licensed rapid
-- transit system".
--
-- Not tapping out is evasion only for a journey travelled; tapping in alone is enough at the attempt stage.
DECLARE Stage IS ONE OF
    `attempting to travel`
    `having travelled`

DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `paid and tapped in and out`
    `did not pay the fare`
    `did not tap in`
    `did not tap out`
    `used a concession without entitlement`
    `used an invalid ticket`

GIVEN `on a covered bus or train` IS A BOOLEAN, `the stage` IS A Stage, `the conduct` IS A Conduct,
      `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual evades the fare` IF
        `on a covered bus or train`
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)
    AND CONSIDER `the conduct`
        WHEN `paid and tapped in and out` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `did not tap out` THEN `the stage` EQUALS `having travelled`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `54(5) -- presumed evasion on inspection`

-- s 54(5): an individual is "presumed, until the contrary is proved, to evade payment" if, when requested by a public transport
-- official, he (a) fails to produce any ticket; (b) produces a concession ticket and then fails to produce evidence of entitlement;
-- (c) or (d) produces a ticket that on inspection is invalid, "and then fails to produce a valid ticket for the journey".
DECLARE Inspection IS ONE OF
    `produced a valid ticket`
    `produced no ticket`
    `produced a concession ticket but no evidence of entitlement`
    `produced a concession ticket with evidence of entitlement`
    `produced an invalid ticket and then no valid ticket`
    `produced an invalid ticket and then a valid ticket`

GIVEN `the inspection` IS A Inspection, `proved the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `evasion is presumed` IF
        (NOT `proved the contrary`)
    AND CONSIDER `the inspection`
        WHEN `produced no ticket` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `produced a concession ticket but no evidence of entitlement` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `produced an invalid ticket and then no valid ticket` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `53 -- the penalty fee`

-- s 53(1): a public transport official who believes on reasonable grounds that an individual is evading or has evaded the fare
-- "may, by notice, offer" an opportunity to pay a penalty fee "of the prescribed amount". (3)-(4) appeal to the Council, which may
-- confirm (and vary the time) or cancel an offer "not equitable"; "every decision on appeal is final". (6) The offer is withdrawn if
-- not paid in time. (8) An individual who pays the penalty fee "cannot be prosecuted for an offence under section 54 or offered
-- composition under section 67".
GIVEN `evaded the fare` IS A BOOLEAN, `was offered a penalty fee` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid it within the time allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may still be prosecuted or offered composition for evasion` IF
        `evaded the fare`
    AND (NOT (`was offered a penalty fee` AND `paid it within the time allowed`))

§§ `52, 57 -- giving name and address`

-- s 57(1): an individual "required by a public transport official to pay a penalty fee" must give name, address and proof of
-- identity; (2) refusing, or "wilfully misstates", is an offence, fine up to $1,000.
-- s 52(2): "It is not an offence for any person to refuse to comply" if the official "refuses to declare his or her office and
-- produce his or her identification card, on demand being made by the person".
GIVEN `required to pay a penalty fee` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused or wilfully misstated` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the official refused to declare office and show the card on demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing to identify oneself is an offence` IF
        `required to pay a penalty fee`
    AND `refused or wilfully misstated`
    AND (NOT `the official refused to declare office and show the card on demand`)

§§ `58 -- arrest without warrant`

-- s 58(1): a public transport official or police officer "may arrest without warrant" an individual he has reason to believe has
-- committed an offence under Part 9, "if the name and address of the individual are unknown" and (a) the individual declines to
-- give them or (b) there is reason to doubt their accuracy. (2)-(3) detention only until they are ascertained, and no longer than
-- necessary to bring him before a court.
GIVEN `reason to believe a Part 9 offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `name and address unknown` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `declines to give them` IS A BOOLEAN, `reason to doubt those given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may arrest without warrant` IF
        `reason to believe a Part 9 offence`
    AND `name and address unknown`
    AND (`declines to give them` OR `reason to doubt those given`)

§§ `56 -- not paying a taxi or ride-hail fare`

-- s 56(1): a passenger of a taxi in a street-hail service, (2) a passenger of a bookable vehicle in a ride-hail service, on a
-- journey "within or partly within Singapore", commits an offence if "without reasonable excuse" he "fails or refuses, at the end of
-- the journey and after a demand by the driver", to pay the fare.
DECLARE Vehicle IS ONE OF
    `a street-hail taxi`
    `a ride-hail bookable vehicle`
    `a public bus`

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle, `journey at least partly in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `driver demanded at the end` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `failed or refused to pay` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not paying the hail fare is an offence` IF
        (`the vehicle` EQUALS `a street-hail taxi` OR `the vehicle` EQUALS `a ride-hail bookable vehicle`)
    AND `journey at least partly in Singapore`
    AND `driver demanded at the end`
    AND `failed or refused to pay`
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `54(2), (3), 56(4), (5) -- repeat offenders`

-- s 54(2)-(3): a repeat offender under s 54(1) is one convicted, before the current conviction, of a qualifying offence: s 54(1) or
-- s 24C(5) "as in force before 29 February 2016". s 56(4): for s 56(1) the earlier offence must be s 56(1) or s 24D as in force
-- before 30 October 2020; s 56(5): for s 56(2), s 56(2) or old s 24D.
--
-- Each limb counts only its own kind. A ride-hail conviction does not make a later street-hail non-payer a repeat offender, and a fare
-- evasion conviction counts for neither.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `bus or train fare evasion (s 54(1))`
    `street-hail non-payment (s 56(1))`
    `ride-hail non-payment (s 56(2))`
    `refusing to identify (s 57(2))`
    `charging an unlawful fare (s 41(7))`
    `licensee offering fares off the pricing policy (s 41(5))`
    `unlicensed ticket payment service (s 64)`

DECLARE EarlierConviction IS ONE OF
    `no earlier conviction`
    `an earlier s 54(1) conviction`
    `an earlier old s 24C(5) conviction`
    `an earlier s 56(1) conviction`
    `an earlier s 56(2) conviction`
    `an earlier old s 24D conviction`
    `an earlier s 57(2) conviction`

GIVEN `the current offence` IS A Offence, `the earlier conviction` IS A EarlierConviction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offender is a repeat offender` IF
    CONSIDER `the current offence`
    WHEN `bus or train fare evasion (s 54(1))` THEN
        `the earlier conviction` EQUALS `an earlier s 54(1) conviction`
        OR `the earlier conviction` EQUALS `an earlier old s 24C(5) conviction`
    WHEN `street-hail non-payment (s 56(1))` THEN
        `the earlier conviction` EQUALS `an earlier s 56(1) conviction`
        OR `the earlier conviction` EQUALS `an earlier old s 24D conviction`
    WHEN `ride-hail non-payment (s 56(2))` THEN
        `the earlier conviction` EQUALS `an earlier s 56(2) conviction`
        OR `the earlier conviction` EQUALS `an earlier old s 24D conviction`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `41, 54, 56, 57, 64 -- maximum punishments`

-- s 54(1): fine up to $1,000; repeat offender, up to $2,000 or 6 months or both. s 56(3): the same. s 57(2): fine up to $1,000.
-- s 41(7): demanding or taking money in contravention of s 41(1)-(4), up to $2,000 or 6 months or both. s 41(5): a street-hail or
-- ride-hail licensee offering fares inconsistent with the pricing policy, up to $100,000 or 6 months or both. s 64: providing a ticket
-- payment service without a licence, up to $50,000 or 6 months or both, and "a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part
-- of a day" the offence continues after conviction.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `is a repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `bus or train fare evasion (s 54(1))` THEN IF `is a repeat offender` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000
    WHEN `street-hail non-payment (s 56(1))` THEN IF `is a repeat offender` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000
    WHEN `ride-hail non-payment (s 56(2))` THEN IF `is a repeat offender` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000
    WHEN `refusing to identify (s 57(2))` THEN 1000
    WHEN `charging an unlawful fare (s 41(7))` THEN 2000
    WHEN `licensee offering fares off the pricing policy (s 41(5))` THEN 100000
    WHEN `unlicensed ticket payment service (s 64)` THEN 50000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `is a repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `bus or train fare evasion (s 54(1))` THEN IF `is a repeat offender` THEN 6 ELSE 0
    WHEN `street-hail non-payment (s 56(1))` THEN IF `is a repeat offender` THEN 6 ELSE 0
    WHEN `ride-hail non-payment (s 56(2))` THEN IF `is a repeat offender` THEN 6 ELSE 0
    WHEN `refusing to identify (s 57(2))` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 6

GIVEN `days or part days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further fine for an unlicensed ticket payment service` MEANS
    5000 * `days or part days continuing after conviction`

§§ `28, 64 -- ticket payment service licence`

-- s 28(1): "A person must not provide or cause to be provided any ticket payment service without a ticket payment service licence."
-- s 2: "ticket payment service" means clearing ticket transactions, or the sale, topping-up, replacement or refund, or management of
-- the use, of a mode of payment for tickets, or a service prescribed by Gazette order.
GIVEN `provides or causes to be provided a ticket payment service` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a ticket payment service licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ticket payment service is unlicensed` IF
    `provides or causes to be provided a ticket payment service` AND (NOT `holds a ticket payment service licence`)

§§ `41 -- charging fares`

-- s 41(1)-(2): a bus or train operator must not demand or take a fare that (a) "is more than the maximum price approved", (b) is
-- inconsistent with the pricing policy, or (c) "is DIFFERENT from the bus fare last published". s 41(3)-(4): for a street-hail or
-- ride-hail fare, only (a) inconsistency with the pricing policy or (b) "is MORE than the ... fare last published". s 41(8): "a strict
-- liability offence". s 41(10): s 41(1) and (7) bind the LTA, public bus operators and their employees.
--
-- A bus or train fare below the published fare contravenes s 41(1)(c); a taxi or ride-hail fare below the published fare does not.
DECLARE FareKind IS ONE OF
    `a bus or train fare`
    `a street-hail or ride-hail fare`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A FareKind, `the fare charged` IS A NUMBER, `the approved maximum` IS A NUMBER, `the last published fare` IS A NUMBER,
      `consistent with the pricing policy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fare contravenes section 41` IF
        (NOT `consistent with the pricing policy`)
    OR  CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `a bus or train fare` THEN
            `the fare charged` > `the approved maximum` OR (NOT (`the fare charged` EQUALS `the last published fare`))
        WHEN `a street-hail or ride-hail fare` THEN
            `the fare charged` > `the last published fare`

§§ `49 and Third Schedule -- the fare adjustment formula`

-- s 49(1): the Council must approve bus and train fares "only in accordance with the fare adjustment formula set out in the Third
-- Schedule". Third Schedule para 1 (as amended by S 669/2025): "0.5 cCPI + 0.4 WI + 0.1 EI - 0.1% + 1.1%", cCPI, WI and EI being the
-- changes in Core CPI, National Average Monthly Earnings (CPF-adjusted) and the Energy Index. Encoded with every term in percent.
-- s 49(2): where the fare charged or approved is less than the maximum permitted, the operator may not demand the excess that year,
-- but "the excess may be claimed (in whole or in part)" in a later year's application; (3) the Council may refuse to add it if no
-- claim is made.
GIVEN `change in core CPI` IS A NUMBER, `change in wages` IS A NUMBER, `change in energy index` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fare adjustment in percent` MEANS
    0.5 * `change in core CPI` + 0.4 * `change in wages` + 0.1 * `change in energy index` - 0.1 + 1.1

GIVEN `maximum permitted adjustment` IS A NUMBER, `adjustment approved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the excess that may be claimed later` MEANS
    IF `adjustment approved` < `maximum permitted adjustment`
    THEN `maximum permitted adjustment` - `adjustment approved`
    ELSE 0

§§ `33, 40 -- Fuel Equalisation Fund penalty and appeal`

-- s 32(1)-(2): a Class 1 bus service licensee or a Part 3 rapid transit licensee must maintain a Fuel Equalisation Fund and "must not
-- withdraw any sum of money from the Fund except with the approval of the Council". s 33(1) (as amended by Act 17 of 2025): a
-- financial penalty "not exceeding $100,000". s 40(1): a licensee may appeal to the Minister "within 14 days of the receipt of the
-- notice"; (2) the decision must be complied with pending the appeal; (4) the Minister's decision is final.
GIVEN `the penalty proposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fund penalty is within the cap` IF
    `the penalty proposed` <= 100000

GIVEN `days since receipt of the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal to the Minister is in time` IF
    `days since receipt of the notice` <= 14

§§ `55(9), (10) -- the smartcard certificate`

-- s 55(5): a certificate of a smartcard reading served on the accused "by the required time" is "conclusive proof"; (9) "required
-- time" means "no less than 56 days before the hearing". (10) Subsections (5) etc. are "subject to" the accused's written notice, at
-- least 28 days before the hearing (or shorter if the court orders or the prosecution agrees), requiring the certifier as a witness or
-- announcing rebuttal evidence.
GIVEN `days before the hearing the certificate was served` IS A NUMBER, `the accused gave a notice in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is conclusive proof` IF
        `days before the hearing the certificate was served` >= 56
    AND (NOT `the accused gave a notice in time`)

§§ `67 -- composition`

-- s 67(1) (as amended by Act 17 of 2025): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of"
-- (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum fine" and (b) "$10,000". (2) On payment no further proceedings are taken.
GIVEN `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`maximum fine for the offence` / 2) 10000
